                    {
                        "name":  "places/ChIJ9bDf1BqpQjQRDjOeRXSNuvg/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25oVlgwTk5UVFZVZUVSM1VUVXlSMVZOU25WdGVFRRAB",
                        "relativePublishTimeDescription":  "10 months ago",
                        "rating":  5,
                        "text":  {
                                     "text":  "This tiny, unassuming roastery café is a hidden gem for lovers of good espresso and pour-over coffee. Despite being part of a chain, it feels very private and cozy indeed!\n\nQuality highlights: a 2-group La Marzocco machine, two Mazzer grinders, 2 Balmuda toasters and a good selection of single-origin beans.\n\nThey also offer Flat White, Sicilian lemon coffee and other lesser-known drinks. Try the cinnamon rolls!\n\nThe owner(?) is very kind and will make special drinks if you ask nicely. Power outlets are available for charging. The only downside: the traditional squat toilet is definitely not for tall people.",
                                     "languageCode":  "en"
                                 },
                        "originalText":  {
                                             "text":  "This tiny, unassuming roastery café is a hidden gem for lovers of good espresso and pour-over coffee. Despite being part of a chain, it feels very private and cozy indeed!\n\nQuality highlights: a 2-group La Marzocco machine, two Mazzer grinders, 2 Balmuda toasters and a good selection of single-origin beans.\n\nThey also offer Flat White, Sicilian lemon coffee and other lesser-known drinks. Try the cinnamon rolls!\n\nThe owner(?) is very kind and will make special drinks if you ask nicely. Power outlets are available for charging. The only downside: the traditional squat toilet is definitely not for tall people.",
                                             "languageCode":  "en"
                                         },
